<Layout title="Bio">
  <div class="content-page">
    <h1>Bio</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Maryna (pronounced Marina) is an artist residing in the Pacific North-West near
        Seattle, surrounded by nature. Though originally from an urban environment, she now
        prefers countryside living while maintaining connections to Seattle's art scene and
        urban exploration.
      </p>

      <p>
        Her core beliefs center on how colors affect people's moods subconsciously, and the
        importance of maintaining healthy happiness and faith in people.
      </p>

      <h2>Interests</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Gardening and visualizing plant compositions</li>
        <li>Home renovation and bringing visions to completion</li>
        <li>Hiking moderate-distance trails</li>
        <li>Psychology</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Education</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          2003-2008 — Southern Ukrainian National Pedagogical University K.D. Ushinsky<br />
          <em>Fine and Decorative and Applied Arts</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          1999-2003 — Republican College of Fine Arts "Alexandru Plămădeală"<br />
          <em>Fine Arts</em>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
